WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.897
Python input validation requires explicit runtime enforcement.

00:00:03.897 --> 00:00:15.587
Type hints, readable models, and framework conventions help developers understand code, but untrusted data still needs to be checked when it enters the application.

00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:26.819
Python will not automatically make external data safe just because the code is annotated or because a request came through a familiar framework.

00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:30.257
Strong validation starts with clear contracts.

00:00:30.257 --> 00:00:40.114
Define expected types, lengths, formats, ranges, required and optional fields, allowed values, nested structures, and business rules before processing data.

00:00:40.114 --> 00:00:44.469
Normalize carefully, parse safely, and validate by context.

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:52.491
A filename, URL, JSON body, environment variable, command argument, and CSV row all require different expectations.

00:00:52.491 --> 00:00:56.847
Safe libraries and framework validators can reduce mistakes.

00:00:56.847 --> 00:01:06.703
Pydantic, Django validators, serializer classes, schema validation, dataclasses with explicit checks, and safe parsers can all help when used intentionally.

00:01:06.703 --> 00:01:15.643
They should be paired with safe database APIs, safe file handling, authorization, output encoding, and careful error handling.

00:01:15.643 --> 00:01:22.290
Validation is powerful, but it is not a complete security model by itself.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.187
The goal is predictable, safe application behavior.

00:01:26.187 --> 00:01:30.083
Test failure cases, not only happy paths.

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:36.272
Include negative tests, boundary tests, malformed input, unexpected encodings, and business-rule violations.

00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:38.794
Log invalid input carefully.

00:01:38.794 --> 00:01:50.484
When Python applications validate inputs consistently and verify assumptions at runtime, they become easier to reason about, easier to test, and safer to operate.
